meta {
  name: Write today's entry with a voice note
  type: http
  seq: 34
}

post {
  url: {{api}}/bonds/{{bondId}}/entries
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "text": "Listen to the rain on the roof.",
    "voiceMediaId": "{{mediaId}}"
  }
}

script:pre-request {
  // A new key on every send, as Write today's entry makes one.
  req.setHeader("Idempotency-Key", require("uuid").v4());
}

script:post-response {
  bru.setVar("entryId", res.body.id);
}

docs {
  An entry with a voice note (ADR-0049): the voice note Media upload intent named with kind VOICE, once Media says it is READY. Its owner only, READY, and on no other entry: anything else is 422 VALIDATION_FAILED on voiceMediaId, one answer whatever the reason, and no entry is written. The 201 carries `voice` with its status READY, a signed URL of an Ogg Opus file and its durationMs; the partner, once the day reveals, sees it PROCESSING with no URL and no length until the owner rules on FR-061 (ADR-0049). A locked entry says nothing of a voice note. An entry may carry a photo (imageMediaId) and a voice note together.

  Bruno's Media upload sends twenty bytes of text, which the pipeline refuses (FAILED): to try this request, upload a real recording of at most 61 seconds (M4A, 3GP, Ogg, WebM, AMR, AAC or WAV; `scripts/smoke.sh`'s voice notes section shows how with curl) as kind VOICE, then set mediaId to its id.
}
